cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "MAES: Multidimensional Algorithmic Evolution System"
message: "If you use this software, please cite as below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Ilarion I."
    family-names: Shapoval
    email: maes.framework@gmail.com
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0004-1851-2036"
repository-code: "https://github.com/MAES-Lab/MAES"
abstract: >
  MAES is a single-file Python multi-agent ALife simulator (NumPy only)
  that studies emergent cognitive ecology, dimensional abduction, and
  communication layers. Built on a hands-off methodology: the experimenter
  sets initial conditions and observes; the simulator does not optimize
  for any goal. Phase 1 empirical study (80 runs, 4 conditions x 20 seeds)
  reports that dimensional abduction (5D->13D) approximately doubles
  ai_peak and yields ~9x increase in species diversity.
  Note: in v1.0 ai_peak was read over a 200-trace window; this measurement
  error is documented in the v3.3 release notes.
keywords:
  - artificial-life
  - multi-agent-systems
  - open-ended-evolution
  - dimensional-abduction
  - cognitive-ecology
  - emergent-communication
  - hands-off-methodology
